# The conditional half of the `.ai/` assessment

The always-check files live in `SKILL.md` step 2. These are the ones whose
relevance depends on what the diff touched. Work the list; do not decide from
memory which ones "probably did not change".

## Check if source changed

- **`.ai/memory.md`** - update if module structure, public interfaces, the data
  model, or release state changed.
- **`.ai/specs/01-architecture.md`** - update if a module was added, the data
  model changed, or a key decision was made.
- **`.ai/specs/dataflow.md`** - update if the way data moves through the system
  changed.
- **`.ai/specs/product-spec.md`** - update the feature status if something
  shipped, got blocked, or was descoped.

## Check if conventions or standards changed

- **`.claude/agents/`** - update the relevant subagent definition if its scope,
  tool allowlist, or model tier changed.
- **`.ai/standards/`** - update if testing or code discipline changed.

## Also keep in lockstep

- **`README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, and any architecture docs under `docs/`** - if
  the repo keeps them, a change to the public surface makes them wrong too.

## What counts as done

A file is assessed when you have either updated it or can say, in one line, why
this diff did not touch what it describes. "I did not look" is not an answer,
and neither is silence - the PR body has to state which files were updated or
explicitly that none needed to be, with the reason.
